amy-sales: Heads up — Acme trial is hitting repeated 429s during the demo right now (started ~10:15 PT). They run parallel chat + embeddings and the chat route is failing every ~10s. Can we swarm? :grimacing:

sam-eng: Can you paste a request id or an example payload + response headers? Need to know if it's per-route or global quota.

amy-sales: Pasting logs from their engineer (sanitized):
```
[2026-03-20T17:15:06Z] 429 from inference.redwood.com/v1/chat - route=chat.default client=acme-trial req=req_7a1a
Headers: Retry-After: 3, X-RateLimit-Type: burst, X-Route-Name: chat
Body: {"error":"rate limit exceeded","quota_remaining":0,"token_budget":0}
[2026-03-20T17:15:16Z] 429 from inference.redwood.com/v1/embeddings - route=embeddings.batch client=acme-trial req=req_7a1b
Headers: Retry-After: 1, X-RateLimit-Type: per-route, X-Route-Name: embeddings
Body: {"error":"rate limit exceeded","quota_remaining":0}
```

jordan-dev: From that it looks like two compounding issues: (1) per-route caps are low for this trial tenant, (2) token_budget is at 0 (so we short-circuit and return 429s when global token budget exhausted). They run 4 concurrent chat streams + batch embeddings every 30s — that will kill a small token_budget.

maria-se: I checked the console for acct `acme-123` (trial): per-route caps -> chat=60rpm, embeddings=30rpm, global requests=200rpm, daily token_budget=100000. The demo's pattern (concurrent sockets + batch embeddings) can easily burn through the token_budget in <30 minutes.

tim-support: Temporary mitigations we can apply right now: increase per-route cap for `chat` to 200rpm, bump token_budget to 500k for 2h, and enable smoothing on the burst window. I can apply a temporary change if sales approves. Also recommend setting fallback model to `small-chat-v1` to reduce token cost under load.

amy-sales: Please do it — customer is on a live demo in 20m. Thanks!

tim-support: Applying now. Will post the change id when done.

deploy-bot: ACTION: quota-change applied by tim-support to acct acme-123. change_id=chg_20260320_001 TTL=2h. Details: chat_rpm=200, token_budget_daily=500000, fallback_model=small-chat-v1.

jordan-dev: Also noticed the client is not honoring `Retry-After` consistently (their log shows repeated immediate retries). Recommend they implement exponential backoff + jitter. Snippet to share: 
```js
async function requestWithRetry(req) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt < 5) {
    const res = await fetch(req);
    if (res.status !== 429) return res;
    const ra = parseInt(res.headers.get('Retry-After')) || Math.pow(2, attempt);
    const waitMs = (ra * 1000) + Math.floor(Math.random() * 200);
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, waitMs));
    attempt++;
  }
  throw new Error('too many 429s');
}
```

maria-se: Filed INF-789 to infra: "Investigate token accounting for trial tenants" — we want to confirm embeddings and chat are being charged exactly as expected (and whether batching miscounts tokens).

amy-sales: Customer confirmed improvement after the quota bump — chat errors dropped. They still want guidance on pricing if they scale this workload. Also asked about a permanent SLA.

sam-eng: Follow-ups: (1) document default trial quotas and recommended demo patterns (we should add a section: avoid >3 concurrent chat streams + large batch embeddings), (2) propose a short-term sales play: temporary quota bump + opt-in Dedicated for customers wanting predictable demo capacity, (3) confirm whether we need to change token accounting for batched embeddings (infra ticket covers that).

maria-se: I'll prep a one-pager for sales on quota-safe demo templates + recommended fallback models.

amy-sales: Great — pls ping me when the one-pager is up. Customer is back on call and seeing stable behavior. :thumbsup:

sam-eng: Schedule a 30m retro with eng+se+support tomorrow to agree on defaults and a permanent fix.

amy-sales: Thanks everyone, closing this swarm for now.
